Looking at the InsertCode method, I can see that:
1. Lines 176-184: If the account's codeHash is changing, it updates the account with the new codeHash
2. Lines 185-192: If EIP-158 is enabled and not genesis, and the account is empty, it performs a "touch"

The crucial logic is in the Commit method. Let me check what happens during commit when an account is "empty". Looking at lines 580-591 in the Commit method:

```csharp
if (releaseSpec.IsEip158Enabled && change.Account.IsEmpty && !isGenesis)
{
    if (isTracing) TraceRemoveEmpty(change);
    SetState(change.Address, null);  // This deletes the account!
    trace?.AddToTrace(change.Address, null);
}
```

So when EIP-158 is enabled and an account is empty (which includes empty code, zero balance, and zero nonce), the account IS deleted during commit.

